mcprack (0.2.6) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix a race in the per-user MCP proxy spawn-on-demand path: concurrent
    cold requests for the same (user, server) pair could race past each
    other with no locking, and the loser's failure-cleanup would delete
    the still-alive winner's pid/meta/healthy_at state files — causing
    502 "failed its startup handshake" errors on every subsequent request
    even while an already-warm client session kept working fine, and
    Admin -> Proxy Instances showing the instance as "not started yet"
    the whole time. Serialize spawn/stop/idle-cleanup per (user, server)
    pair with a cross-process file lock. (GitHub issue #1)

 -- CyberVitexus <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0200

mcprack (0.2.5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Integrate dbconfig-common: the installer now prompts for the database
    engine (sqlite3, PostgreSQL, or MySQL) and connection details the
    standard Debian way, instead of hardcoding sqlite in postinst.
  * Run `flask db upgrade` (Alembic) automatically in postinst on every
    install and upgrade, rather than relying solely on `db.create_all()`.
  * Automatically create an initial `admin` account with a random password
    (saved to /etc/mcprack/admin-credentials) when no admin user exists yet.

 -- CyberVitexus <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0200

mcprack (0.2.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Automatically create missing database tables (such as `audit_log_entries`)
    on application startup to prevent 500 errors when upgrading existing databases.

 -- CyberVitexus <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Mon, 27 Jul 2026 00:43:00 +0200

mcprack (0.2.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Harden the per-user MCP proxy: bounded handshake probe with auto-
    heal, deterministic JSON-RPC errors on upstream failure,
    unauthenticated /health endpoint, admin stdio 'Test' action, and a
    server-subscriptions view.
  * Implement database-backed audit logging with event retention management
    (`flask audit-archive`).
  * Add experimental OpenTelemetry (OTEL) traces and metrics support with
    admin setup wizard and Grafana dashboards.

 -- CyberVitexus <info@vitexsoftware.cz>  Sun, 26 Jul 2026 17:04:12 +0200

